# SMILE 7.1.0 Release Notes

Welcome to **SMILE 7.1.0**! This release unifies high-performance JVM machine learning with the next generation of agentic data science. Building on the 7.0 architecture, **SMILE 7.1.0** introduces autonomous desktop automation, multi-agent orchestration, model-agnostic KernelSHAP explainability with interactive visualizations, a pure-Java BLAS/LAPACK fallback engine, four tailored SMILE Serve container flavors (`latest`, `-gpu`, `-native`, `-micro`), high-throughput LLM serving with batched Multi-Token Prediction (MTP) speculative decoding, native Kotlin and Scala 3 notebook kernels, an extensive productivity and research skills suite, time series forecasting (ARIMA/ARMA), OS keychain credential storage, and comprehensive stability hardening across Studio, Serve, and the Agent harness.

---

## ✨ New Features

### 🤖 AI Agents & Desktop Automation
- **🖥️ Desktop Operator Agent (`@chuck`)**:
  - Introduced Chuck, a specialized desktop automation agent capable of interacting directly with GUI applications via screenshot analysis, mouse navigation, and keyboard control.
  - Safe desktop automation pipeline with coordinate mapping, interactive user confirmation, and automatic session bounds.
- **👔 Chief of Staff Agent (`@frank`)**:
  - Added Frank to coordinate multi-agent teams, synthesize status reports across active agents, track project priorities, and lead cross-agent briefings.
- **📣 Evangelist (`@julien`) & Sales (`@mike`) Workspace Integration**:
  - Added localized welcome and capability banners for Evangelist and Sales agents across all supported workspace locales, expanded the Java and Python Coder capability overviews, and organized agent tabs in the Studio panel.
- **Dynamic Agent Catalog**:
  - Studio discovers and loads agent personas dynamically from configuration specifications, with clean peer-to-peer delegation and request queuing.

### ⚡ High-Performance LLM & Model Serving (`smile-serve`)
- **Batched Multi-Token Prediction (MTP) Speculative Decoding**:
  - Implemented high-throughput batched MTP speculative decoding with persistent per-request draft histories, enabled by default in `smile.serve`.
  - Accelerated generation with fused DeltaNet window operations, eager FlashInfer attention, and CUDA graph verification for low-latency token generation.
- **Interactive SHAP Explanations in API & Web UI**:
  - Native SHAP explanation payloads (`TreeSHAP`, `LinearSHAP`, and `KernelSHAP`) in REST and streaming inference responses with clean 3-decimal formatting and zero overhead when unrequested.
  - Interactive SHAP explanation pane in the Predictions panel supporting **Waterfall**, **Force**, and **Decision** plots for both 1D regression and 2D multi-class classification outputs, updating dynamically as you click rows.
  - Per-request KernelSHAP tuning via `?samples` and `?ridge` query parameters (or `shapSamples`, `shapRidge`, and nested `shap` payload fields) and inline **Samples** and **Ridge** controls in the Web UI.
- **Four Container Image Flavors (`latest`, `-gpu`, `-native`, `-micro`)**:
  - **`Dockerfile.micro` (`-micro`, ~205 MB)**: Single-stage UBI 10 micro GraalVM native image built with the `micro` profile for lightweight, inference-only deployments (`.sml` and ONNX models + Web UI, without chat, auth, or JDBC overhead).
  - **`Dockerfile.native` (`-native`, ~375 MB)**: GraalVM native image with CPU chat powered by ONNX Runtime GenAI.
  - **`Dockerfile` (`latest`, ~575 MB)**: Lean CPU JVM image with ONNX Runtime GenAI support for CPU chat.
  - **`Dockerfile.gpu` (`-gpu`)**: Self-contained multi-stage build with full GPU/CUDA and S3 blob storage support.
- **Pluggable Blob Storage SPI & `local` Profile**:
  - Extracted S3 blob storage into an optional build-time plugin (`serve-plugins/blob-s3` and `serve-plugins/blob-spi`, selectable via `-Pserve.plugins=...`) to keep the AWS SDK out of CPU and native images.
  - Added a dedicated `local` Quarkus profile (embedded H2 in the model directory without PostgreSQL) and scoped `quarkus-jdbc-postgresql` to `prod`.
- **Dynamic Model Loading & Control APIs**:
  - Dynamically load and unload models on the fly via `POST /api/v1/models/load`.
  - Added real-time telemetry, model control, and health endpoints (`/smile/{id}`, `/onnx/{id}`, and `/q/health`).
  - Support for ONNX Runtime 1.30, ONNX Runtime GenAI models (including Phi-4 mini), LibTorch 2.14.1, and automatic KV-cache precision selection (`auto`).
- **Centralized Prometheus Metrics API**:
  - **`GET /q/metrics`:** Single scrape target formatted according to standard Prometheus text specifications.
  - **Multidimensional Labeling:** Every time-series metric carries a `model_id` label, allowing unified visualization dashboards (e.g., Grafana) with dynamic multi-tenant filtering.
  - **Microsecond Precision & Non-blocking Execution:** Latency observations, throughput gauges, and cache counters are recorded with sub-millisecond fidelity via Micrometer using atomic primitives and lightweight histograms.

### 📚 Expanded Skills Suite
- **Comprehensive Document Processing**:
  - **Excel (`excel-processing`)**: Read, analyze, create, and format spreadsheets (`.xlsx`, `.csv`) with support for formulas, styles, and embedded charts.
  - **Word (`word-processing`)**: Parse, edit, and generate Microsoft Word documents (`.docx`) with precise layout and typography control.
  - **PDF (`pdf-processing`)**: Extract, analyze, and render publication-quality PDF reports and slide decks.
- **Research & Development Skills**:
