  - **Skill Creator (`skill-creator`)**: Interactive creation, evaluation, and optimization of custom agent skills.

### 📓 Interactive Notebooks & Polyglot Data Science
- **🚀 Native Kotlin Scripting Kernel**:
  - Interactive Kotlin notebooks (`.kts`) powered by the Kotlin Custom Scripting Host API with full access to SMILE algorithms.
- **⚡ AST-Aware Scala 3 Evaluation**:
  - `ScalaKernel` parses code using the Scala 3 compiler to evaluate complete top-level classes, multi-line blocks, and closures without timeouts or truncation.
- **Interactive Welcome & Release Notes**:
  - Replaced the blank starting file with an interactive `Welcome` tutorial and dedicated `Release Notes` viewer.

### 📈 Machine Learning, Analytics & Core Engine
- **Model-Agnostic KernelSHAP (`smile.feature.importance.KernelSHAP`)**:
  - Brought SHAP feature attributions to all DataFrame and linear models—including Logistic Regression, LDA, QDA, RDA, Fisher, MLP, SVM, RBF networks, OLS, Lasso, ElasticNet, Ridge, and Gaussian Process models—alongside existing TreeSHAP support.
  - Uses exact coalition enumeration for small feature sets, priority symmetric shell enumeration with antithetic paired sampling for larger feature sets, and single-factorization multi-output Cholesky/SVD solvers.
  - Added `KernelSHAP.Options` overloads to `shap(...)` and `infer(...)` on `SHAP`, `DataFrameClassifier`, `DataFrameRegression`, `ClassificationModel`, and `RegressionModel` for inference-time tuning without rebuilding background state.
- **Pure-Java BLAS & LAPACK Fallback (`smile.linalg`, `smile.tensor`)**:
  - `smile.tensor` now works out of the box on machines without native OpenBLAS or system BLAS/LAPACK installed instead of failing with `UnsatisfiedLinkError`.
  - Implemented pure-Java Level-1/2/3 BLAS (`JBlas`) and LAPACK decompositions and solvers (`JLapack`: LU, Cholesky, QR, SVD, symmetric/general EVD, packed symmetric, and banded solvers) for both `Float64` and `Float32`.
  - Added `NativeLibrary.isBlasAvailable()` and `NativeLibrary.isLapackAvailable()` probes, plus backend selection via the `smile.linalg.backend` system property or `SMILE_LINALG_BACKEND` environment variable (`auto`, `native`, or `java`).
- **Time Series Analysis (ARIMA & ARMA)**:
  - Added `smile.timeseries.ARIMA` supporting arbitrary differencing, stationary transformation, and recursive multi-step forecasting.
  - Added model selection diagnostics: Gaussian log-likelihood, AIC, BIC, RSS, and coefficient $t$-test tables.
  - Added pure MA fitting via Hannan-Rissanen stage-2 least squares in `smile.timeseries.ARMA`.
- **Unit-Hypercube Hyperparameter Optimization (HPO)**:
  - Added `smile.hpo.ParameterSpace` supporting continuous, integer, and discrete search spaces normalized into a unit hypercube $[0, 1]^d$, with uniform candidate sampling and elite local perturbations.
- **Local Outlier Factor (LOF) Anomaly Detection**:
  - Density-based anomaly detection via `smile.anomaly.LOF<T>` across arbitrary metric spaces.
- **Tree Ensemble Feature Selection**:
  - Introduced `smile.feature.selection.EnsembleSelection` to score, rank, and threshold feature importance from Random Forests, Gradient Boosted Trees, and Decision Trees.
- **Java 25 Spark Module**:
  - Modernized `spark` module rewritten in pure Java 25.

### 🔌 Extensibility & Marketplace
- **Claude Code-Style Plugin Marketplace**:
  - Integrated plugin marketplace dialog in Studio, seeded with official plugin catalogs and discovery tools.
- **Scoped MCP Integration**:
  - Support for Model Context Protocol (MCP) servers with per-agent scoping via `x-smile-agents` and automatic omission of redundant provider tools via `x-smile-provides`.

